        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: the event determination is blocked by missing records\n\nThe available records identify the requested work order and Pending Close time, but **do not establish whether a cost event was created afterward**. The supporting cost-event input returned “Supporting input was not staged for this assignment.”\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine–DeKoven / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** — timezone not specified |\n| Source transaction | Unavailable from the supplied records |\n| Event amount | Unavailable |\n| Exact event-created time | Unavailable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Cannot determine without the event details** |\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B states that newly created transactions falling in or before a **Pending Close** period are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting and are processed after the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue to be processed. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing.\n\nAccordingly, an ordinary manufacturing cost transaction newly created after the timestamp above should be held while the period remains Pending Close. The missing event type, timestamp, and recorded status prevent an event-specific consistency conclusion.\n\n**Sources:** `state.db`, `work_orders` and `cost_periods`; Oracle 26B documentation, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225.\n\nNo database records were changed. The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_fe2ee36503ab/audit-report.json`. Missing evidence should **not** be interpreted as confirmation that no late event occurred.",
